## 6. Diagnostics, metrics, statistics

### 6.1 Diagnostics (also used for early stopping of bridges)
- Bridge residual score: draw 100 random Fourier features g_j of the standardized
  instrument input; report max_j | En[R_i g_j(.)] | / sd(R). Early-stop h on this
  (validation fold), analogously for q with S_i.
- q sanity: En[1{T = t_k} q_hat_k] (target 1); max weight; ESS_k = (sum w)^2 / sum w^2.
- Proxy strength: regress X out of W and V (linear), CCA on residuals; report top-2
  canonical correlations (rho_min = 2nd one).
- Arm overlap: per-arm counts; distribution of min_k pi_hat_k(X).

### 6.2 Metrics
- PEHE = sqrt( mean_i mean_{k>=1} ( tau_hat_k(x_i) - tau_k(x_i) )^2 ).
- ATE error = mean_{k>=1} | ATE_hat_k - ATE_k |.
- Policy value (synthetic/semi-synth): value of argmax_k mu_hat_k(x) under TRUE potential
  outcomes. Real data: IPW value with ONE shared cross-fitted propensity model used for
  ALL methods (state direction of "better" explicitly in the report).

### 6.3 Statistical protocol
10 seeds; paired Wilcoxon signed-rank AND paired t-test vs the best competing method per
(scenario, metric); Benjamini–Hochberg across scenarios; per-seed scatter saved with every
headline table; seed-bootstrap 95% CIs on means. `eval/stats.py` implements all of this
and every table generator must call it.

