## 7. Unit tests (pytest; all must pass before any experiment is trusted)

1. `test_kernel_ustat_matches_naive`: batch of 32, U-statistic loss equals a double-loop
   reference within 1e-6.
2. `test_bridge_closed_form`: DGP 3.1, n = 8000, single seed: linear probe of h_hat
   achieves R^2 > 0.95 vs h_true; |ATE_hat - 2| < 0.15.
3. `test_q_moment`: En[1{T=k} q_hat_k] in [0.9, 1.1] for both arms (DGP 3.1).
4. `test_dr_product_bias`: with h_true and corrupted q (or vice versa), ATE error at
   n = 8000 remains < 0.15 (double robustness smoke test).
5. `test_crossfit_no_leakage`: assert every prediction index was absent from its
   training folds (bookkeeping test with planted markers).
6. `test_dgp_truth`: oracle tau plugged into PEHE gives 0; S1 counterfactual law matches
   Monte-Carlo simulation of the DGP (KS test p > 0.01).
7. `test_dr_fallback_equals_proximal_when_no_confounding`: c_U = 0 in S1, the two modes'
   ATE estimates differ by < 2 * pooled SE.

