## 8. Milestones (strict order; produce REPORT.md at each gate)

- M0: repo skeleton + DGPs + unit tests 1, 5, 6 green.
- M1: bridges + estimator; tests 2, 3, 4, 7 green; E1 PASS.  <- hard gate: do not
  proceed to baselines/benchmarks until E1 passes.
- M2: E2 PASS.
- M3: baselines + E3; if E3 FAIL, debug via Sec 6.1 diagnostics and report findings.
- M4: E4 (linear-POR gate first), E5.
- M5: generator + E6, E7, E8; final consolidated LaTeX tables and figures.

## 9. Do-NOT list

- Do not create any joint loss across stages or any learned loss weights.
- Do not implement "learned proxies" of any kind.
- Do not tune anything on test data or on causal ground truth.
- Do not headline oracle-supervised variants against baselines (oracle curves are
  upper-bound references only, drawn as dashed lines).
- Do not silently change DGP constants, thresholds, or acceptance criteria; any deviation
  goes to DECISIONS.md with justification.
- Do not fabricate results for missing baselines; mark "did not run" with the reason.